  "content": {
    "id": "p17-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "Evaluate $a+\\frac{1}{a}$ for these values of $a$:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p17-q12-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$1+\\sqrt{2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2\\sqrt{2}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{a}&=\\frac{1}{1+\\sqrt{2}}\\times\\frac{1-\\sqrt{2}}{1-\\sqrt{2}}\\\\\\frac{1}{a}&=\\frac{1-\\sqrt{2}}{1-2}=\\sqrt{2}-1\\\\a+\\frac{1}{a}&=1+\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{2}-1\\\\a+\\frac{1}{a}&=2\\sqrt{2}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q12-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$2-\\sqrt{3}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$4$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{a}&=\\frac{1}{2-\\sqrt{3}}\\times\\frac{2+\\sqrt{3}}{2+\\sqrt{3}}\\\\\\frac{1}{a}&=\\frac{2+\\sqrt{3}}{4-3}=2+\\sqrt{3}\\\\a+\\frac{1}{a}&=2-\\sqrt{3}+2+\\sqrt{3}\\\\a+\\frac{1}{a}&=4\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q12-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\frac{3-\\sqrt{3}}{3+\\sqrt{3}}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$4$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}a+\\frac{1}{a}&=\\frac{3-\\sqrt{3}}{3+\\sqrt{3}}+\\frac{3+\\sqrt{3}}{3-\\sqrt{3}}\\\\a+\\frac{1}{a}&=\\frac{(3-\\sqrt{3})^2+(3+\\sqrt{3})^2}{(3+\\sqrt{3})(3-\\sqrt{3})}\\\\a+\\frac{1}{a}&=\\frac{9-6\\sqrt{3}+3+9+6\\sqrt{3}+3}{9-3}\\\\a+\\frac{1}{a}&=\\frac{24}{6}\\\\a+\\frac{1}{a}&=4\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q12-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\frac{\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{2-x}}{\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{2-x}}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{2}{x-1}$\n\nCombine the reciprocal fractions using the conjugate product in the denominator.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}a+\\frac{1}{a}&=\\frac{\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{2-x}}{\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{2-x}}+\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{2-x}}{\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{2-x}}\\\\a+\\frac{1}{a}&=\\frac{(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{2-x})^2+(\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{2-x})^2}{(\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{2-x})(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{2-x})}\\\\a+\\frac{1}{a}&=\\frac{x+2\\sqrt{x(2-x)}+2-x+x-2\\sqrt{x(2-x)}+2-x}{x-(2-x)}\\\\a+\\frac{1}{a}&=\\frac{4}{2x-2}\\\\a+\\frac{1}{a}&=\\frac{2}{x-1}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe original expression is defined for $0\\le x\\le2$, with $x\\ne1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      }
    ]
  },
